Current Engram binary for pinned TermAl live runs (Fable2, 2026-10-05 about 05:51Z; supersedes 690c5acf for bd2c5af and 2d0f7204 for 3abe2b2). Engram 92fc3d0 (bundle 11: w-aa27ad3c08ba + w-0717569bf3df) is installed: exe sha256 eb17bcf36fa71302a6cb5570f8880ff382831ec1705cc5d9fec9db6e4633fbbc, build_fingerprint ae540744b41c0776b1766a76246ccd4614754c956c3ef5844d14346eadc3d41c (install notice: Engram::Fable, TermAl mailbox ebe242f7 #667). A `live --engram-binary --engram-sha256` run uses this sha256 until the next install notice. Behaviour since bd2c5af:
- opening a brand-new store is atomic;
- a store still cold after one restart refuses as a typed busy (SQLite BUSY), which TermAl maps like any SQLite error;
- next's changes section lists same-session changes made as another kind or by another actor.
No schema or wire change. Running MCP sessions pick it up at the next TermAl restart (not urgent); new CLI processes have it now.
